  "scenario": "**Character interaction:** Tiffany Miller, Mr. Miller’s adult daughter, stops you in the hallway at the start of your shift.\n\n**Timeline:** 7 a.m. Mr. Miller arrived in the ED 48 hours ago.\n\n**Reason for the conversation:** Tiffany has been at his bedside overnight and wants to know what is happening.\n\n**Sign-out you received.**\n\n> **Mr. Frank Miller, 78.** Admitted 48 h ago with choledocholithiasis: 2 days of RUQ/epigastric pain, longer than his usual short colicky episodes, with nausea, dark urine, light stools; daughter noticed his eyes turning yellow. No prior abdominal surgery. US: CBD 9 mm with a distal stone. **Repeat labs this morning are stable, no sign of cholangitis or pancreatitis.** His vitals are stable and he has been afebrile. His pain is well controlled on IV meds. IV fluids are running. He has been **NPO since midnight for an ERCP today** he was bumped yesterday by urgent cases and is on today’s add-on list; there is no time yet. He is still waiting on an inpatient bed. And his Daughter, Tiffany, has been at his bedside.",
